<title>USA: Missouri direct hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Missouri direct hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>JEFFERSON CITY 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barrows and Gilts $1.00 higher than Friday's close. Demand good and Supply moderate to light. Top $59.00 per cwt. - USDA</p>
<p>US 1-3    230-260 lbs    57.00-59.00</p>
<p>US 1-2    210-220 lbs    54.00-57.00</p>
<p>US 1-3    220-230 lbs    56.00-57.00</p>
<p>US 2-3    260-270 lbs    56.00-57.00</p>
<p>	    270-280 lbs    55.00-56.00</p>
<p>Sows steady to 1.00 higher. Top 52.00.</p>
<p>US 1-3    300-500 lbs    41.00-44.00</p>
<p>	   over 500 lbs    48.00-52.00</p>
<p>Estimated receipts  7,500, Week ago  7,723, Year ago 11,207.</p>
<p>Friday's actual receipts  5,807.</p>
<p>Saturday's actual receipts 2,635.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
